comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T19:42:18.033Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-07: searched all PM statuses for GH-930, duplicates status all, unknown status, and zero-item duplicate scans. Closed pm-mp49 fixed the package-owned dedupe-audit rejection path and pm-i02t covers list/search all-status semantics; neither covers the core duplicates false-clean acceptance regression, so this distinct item preserves those typed relationships."
  "2026-08-07T19:42:58.576Z","harness:codex","GitHub report: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/930; backlink comment: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/930#issuecomment-5221326386."
  "2026-08-08T16:46:57.238Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence (2026-08-08): full release pipeline reached the pre-commit hosted-review boundary after all local gates passed. Exact coverage: 460 files, 7072 tests, statements 50283/50283, branches 36738/36738, functions 10330/10330, lines 48684/48684. Static quality/docstrings, docs/skills, SDK surface, package boundary/parity, token/context/retrieval/tracker/security/version, packed npx (13 packages), and 88-command temporary package-first dogfood all passed. Manual packed external acceptance also passed all-status duplicates, 13 unique package rows with aliases, SDK direction-independent merge, package-manage output resolution, merge install, and health classification. The remaining greptile gate refusal is expected before a reviewable commit: no committed code changes to review against main."
  "2026-08-08T17:27:20.425Z","harness:codex","Review feedback: CodeRabbit found two valid contract gaps: mixed all plus concrete statuses bypass validation, and filters.statuses reports raw rather than canonical runtime statuses. Reopened the canonical GH-930 item for one shared normalization fix and regression proof."
  "2026-08-08T17:41:03.455Z","harness:codex","Review fix evidence: one normalization path now validates every concrete status, refuses mixed all-plus-concrete filters, applies canonical runtime values, and returns those exact values in filters.statuses. Direct SDK plus CLI integration tests pass; full suite is 460 files / 7,072 tests at exact 100/100/100/100."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-08T16:49:44.529Z","harness:codex",All-status duplicate searches need an explicit unrestricted semantic plus a returned filter receipt so agents can trust that closed historical lineage was included.
